---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Post-Labor Economics — a_e.s_" description="A visual systems model of automation, labor displacement, and the demand crisis driving new economic agency beyond wages alone." theme="archive">

  <style>
    .ple-wrap {
      --ple-accent: #c4965a;
      --ple-accent-soft: rgba(196,150,90,0.12);
      --ple-line: rgba(196,150,90,0.22);
    }
    .ple-hero {
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
      border: 1px solid var(--ple-line);
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tone-surface) 80%, var(--ple-accent-soft));
      padding: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2rem);
      margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
    }
    .ple-kicker { font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ple-accent); font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
    .ple-hero h1 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 0.98; letter-spacing: -0.04em; }
    .ple-hero p { margin: 0.9rem 0 0; max-width: 72ch; color: var(--tone-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
    .ple-watermark { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; pointer-events: none; user-select: none; overflow: hidden; }
    .ple-watermark span { font-size: clamp(4rem, 14vw, 9rem); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(196,150,90,0.06); white-space: nowrap; transform: rotate(-8deg); }

    .ple-main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr; gap: 1.2rem; align-items: start; }

    .ple-card { border: 1px solid var(--ple-line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--tone-surface); padding: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
    .ple-card:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .ple-card h2 { font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 1rem; }

    .ple-flow { display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; }
    .ple-node { border: 1px solid var(--ple-line); border-radius: 12px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tone-surface) 70%, var(--tone-bg) 30%); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 600; text-align: center; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .ple-node small { display: block; margin-top: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--tone-muted); line-height: 1.35; }
    .ple-arrow { text-align: center; color: var(--ple-accent); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1; margin: -0.1rem 0; }

    .ple-stakeholders { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; }
    .ple-stake { border: 1px solid var(--ple-line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 0.9rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tone-surface) 60%, var(--tone-bg) 40%); }
    .ple-stake h3 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
    .ple-stake p { margin: 0; color: var(--tone-muted); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.5; }

    .ple-contradiction { border: 1px dashed var(--ple-accent); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--ple-accent-soft); padding: 1rem 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
    .ple-contradiction strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--ple-accent); letter-spacing: 0.03em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.72rem; }
    .ple-contradiction p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; }

    .ple-mix { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }
    .ple-mix-group-label { font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.84rem; margin: 0 0 0.55rem; }
    .ple-bar-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 72px 1fr 32px; gap: 0.6rem; align-items: center; font-size: 0.82rem; }
    .ple-bar-track { height: 14px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tone-bg) 70%, var(--ple-accent-soft)); border-radius: 999px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--ple-line); }
    .ple-bar-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 999px; }
    .ple-bar-fill.wages    { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #8d6733, #c39b62); }
    .ple-bar-fill.property { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #bda98a, #d7c5ab); }
    .ple-bar-fill.transfer { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #8a826f, #b3a891); }
    .ple-divider { height: 1px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--ple-line), transparent); margin: 0.9rem 0; }

    .ple-agency { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0.7rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
    .ple-pill { border: 1px solid var(--ple-line); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.7rem 0.5rem; text-align: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.8rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tone-surface) 70%, var(--tone-bg) 30%); }

    .ple-source-note { border-top: 1px solid var(--ple-line); padding-top: 1rem; margin-top: 1.8rem; color: var(--tone-muted); font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.6; }

    @media (max-width: 800px) { .ple-main { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .ple-stakeholders, .ple-agency { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
    @media (max-width: 520px) { .ple-stakeholders { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .ple-agency { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .ple-bar-row { grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr 26px; } }
  </style>

  <div class="ple-wrap">
    <section class="ple-hero">
      <div class="ple-watermark" aria-hidden="true"><span>DAVID SHAPIRO</span></div>
      <div style="position:relative;z-index:1;">
        <p class="ple-kicker">System View</p>
        <h1>Post-Labor Economics</h1>
        <p>A visual model of the central argument: automation raises productive capacity while undermining wage-based distribution, creating a demand crisis that pushes the economy toward new forms of economic agency beyond wages alone.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="ple-main">
      <div>
        <article class="ple-card">
          <h2>Causal chain</h2>
          <div class="ple-flow">
            <div class="ple-node">Automation improves<small>better · faster · cheaper · safer</small></div>
            <div class="ple-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="ple-node">Labor substitution<small>human work is displaced or narrowed</small></div>
            <div class="ple-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="ple-node">Wages lose central economic role<small>labor income becomes less reliable as the main distribution channel</small></div>
            <div class="ple-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="ple-node">Consumer purchasing power weakens<small>less money reaches people through work</small></div>
            <div class="ple-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="ple-node">Aggregate demand destabilizes<small>productive capacity rises while customers lose spending power</small></div>
            <div class="ple-arrow">↓</div>
            <div class="ple-node">Wage-centered social contract cracks<small>the old employment bargain stops organizing the economy well</small></div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ple-card">
          <h2>Stakeholder pressures</h2>
          <div class="ple-stakeholders">
            <div class="ple-stake"><h3>Consumers</h3><p>Need money in the account, purchasing power, and real economic agency.</p></div>
            <div class="ple-stake"><h3>Businesses</h3><p>Want lower labor costs, but still need customers able to buy goods and services.</p></div>
            <div class="ple-stake"><h3>Government</h3><p>Needs stability, legitimacy, tax capacity, and a workable distribution system.</p></div>
            <div class="ple-stake"><h3>Banks</h3><p>Need depositors with balances, transaction volume, repayment capacity, and financial circulation.</p></div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <div class="ple-contradiction">
          <strong>Core contradiction</strong>
          <p>Automation can expand output and efficiency while simultaneously shrinking wage-distributed purchasing power. The system becomes more productive, yet less able to distribute access through employment alone.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <article class="ple-card">
          <h2>Income mix shift</h2>
          <div class="ple-mix">
            <div>
              <p class="ple-mix-group-label">Old mix</p>
              <div class="ple-bar-row"><span>Wages</span><div class="ple-bar-track"><div class="ple-bar-fill wages" style="width:60%"></div></div><span>60</span></div>
              <div class="ple-bar-row"><span>Property</span><div class="ple-bar-track"><div class="ple-bar-fill property" style="width:20%"></div></div><span>20</span></div>
              <div class="ple-bar-row"><span>Transfers</span><div class="ple-bar-track"><div class="ple-bar-fill transfer" style="width:20%"></div></div><span>20</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="ple-divider"></div>
            <div>
              <p class="ple-mix-group-label">Proposed shift</p>
              <div class="ple-bar-row"><span>Wages</span><div class="ple-bar-track"><div class="ple-bar-fill wages" style="width:20%"></div></div><span>20</span></div>
              <div class="ple-bar-row"><span>Property</span><div class="ple-bar-track"><div class="ple-bar-fill property" style="width:60%"></div></div><span>60</span></div>
              <div class="ple-bar-row"><span>Transfers</span><div class="ple-bar-track"><div class="ple-bar-fill transfer" style="width:20%"></div></div><span>20</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ple-card">
          <h2>Economic agency model</h2>
          <div class="ple-agency">
            <div class="ple-pill">Labor Rights</div>
            <div class="ple-pill">Property Rights</div>
            <div class="ple-pill">Voting Rights</div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--tone-muted);margin:0;line-height:1.55;">If labor rights weaken as the main way people access the economy, property and transfer systems have to expand without eroding democratic legitimacy.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="ple-card">
          <h2>Solution stack</h2>
          <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--tone-muted);margin:0;line-height:1.6;">UBI or transfers can stabilize the floor, but the broader structural move is toward wider ownership: shares, public or sovereign funds, trusts, co-ops, dividends, and other systems that distribute property-linked income more broadly.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="ple-card">
          <h2>Human work that may persist</h2>
          <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--tone-muted);margin:0;line-height:1.6;">Some roles remain harder to automate because they depend on liability, law, trust, lived experience, or social presence rather than output alone.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="ple-source-note">Conceptual framing draws from David Shapiro's post-labor economics lectures and related arguments.</p>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
